{
    "technical_and_design_decisions": [
        "Language: Go, aligning with Hyperledger Fabric's primary ecosystem and the SDK.",
        "Architecture: Design the library as a set of stateless, pure functions that operate on existing protobuf-serialized Config blocks/transactions. This aligns with the 'fit-for-purpose library' requirement and the reference tutorial's workflow.",
        "Core API Design: Expose functions that accept a serialized `common.Config` or `common.ConfigEnvelope` and return a `common.ConfigUpdateEnvelope` (or the bytes for it). This keeps the library focused on configuration delta generation, not network submission or signing.",
        "Dependency: The library will depend on the `hyperledger/fabric` core protobuf definitions and the `fabric-protos-go` binding for Go. It will not depend on the Fabric SDK's high-level abstractions to keep it lightweight.",
        "Certificate Handling: For U4 (Add Root CA), implement a minimal validation function that uses the `crypto/x509` package to parse the certificate and check the `KeyUsageCertSign` bit in the `KeyUsage` extension. Other validation is deferred to Fabric's MSP at runtime.",
        "Documentation: GoDoc comments will serve as the primary documentation (U5, U6). Examples will be runnable testable examples within the package, demonstrating multi-step workflows."
    ],
    "assumptions": [
        "The developer (myself) has intermediate-to-advanced knowledge of Go, Hyperledger Fabric's configuration system (channel config protobufs), and the MSP configuration structure.",
        "A development environment with the necessary Go toolchain and dependencies (like `go mod`) is already set up.",
        "The library will target Fabric v1.4.x APIs and protobuf definitions as per the referenced documentation links.",
        "The signature workflow (mentioned in acceptances) is out-of-scope for this library; the library produces a ready-to-sign `ConfigUpdateEnvelope`. The example (U5) will show how to use a hypothetical signing function.",
        "Existing anchor peers (U7) and orderer configuration (U8) can be extracted by parsing the standard protobuf `ChannelGroup` structure within the config. No direct Fabric peer query is involved.",
        "Error handling will follow Go idioms, returning descriptive errors. No custom error types are needed beyond this.",
        "All unit tests will be written in Go using the standard `testing` package."
    ],
    "activities": [
        {
            "activity_id": "A1",
            "activity_name": "Project Initialization & Core Structure",
            "activity_description": "Set up the Go module, define the package structure, and design core data structures (e.g., `ChannelConfig`, helper types) and interfaces. Create stubs for the public API functions.",
            "most_likely_effort": 1
        },
        {
            "activity_id": "A2",
            "activity_name": "Implement Add Anchor Peer (U1)",
            "activity_description": "Implement the function to parse an existing config, locate the `Application.ChannelGroup.Orgs[orgName].Values[AnchorPeers]` config value, add the specified peer to the list, and compute the ConfigUpdate.",
            "most_likely_effort": 2
        },
        {
            "activity_id": "A3",
            "activity_name": "Implement Remove Anchor Peer (U2)",
            "activity_description": "Implement the complementary function to remove a specified anchor peer from the list in the Org config value. Shares significant logic with Add Anchor Peer.",
            "most_likely_effort": 2
        },
        {
            "activity_id": "A4",
            "activity_name": "Implement Certificate Revocation (U3)",
            "activity_description": "Implement function to locate the MSP config for a specified org within the config, access the `FabricMSPConfig`, and append the provided certificate's serial number and AKI to the `RevocationList` field. Requires understanding of MSP proto structure.",
            "most_likely_effort": 3
        },
        {
            "activity_id": "A5",
            "activity_name": "Implement Add Root CA Certificate (U4)",
            "activity_description": "Implement function to add a new root CA certificate to an MSP's `RootCertificate` field. Include the minimal validation logic (parse cert, check KeyUsageCertSign).",
            "most_likely_effort": 2
        },
        {
            "activity_id": "A6",
            "activity_name": "Implement Get Existing Anchor Peers (U7)",
            "activity_description": "Implement a helper function that parses the config to retrieve the current list of anchor peers for a given organization. This is a read-only operation.",
            "most_likely_effort": 1
        },
        {
            "activity_id": "A7",
            "activity_name": "Implement Get Orderer Configuration (U8)",
            "activity_description": "Implement a helper function that extracts the `Orderer` configuration (e.g., batch timeout, block size) from the `ChannelGroup`'s `Orderer` section and returns it as a Go struct for easy manipulation.",
            "most_likely_effort": 2
        },
        {
            "activity_id": "A8",
            "activity_name": "Write Documentation Examples (U5, U6)",
            "activity_description": "Write comprehensive GoDoc examples demonstrating: 1) An idiomatically updating channel configuration (including multiple changes and state management) and signing the envelope (U5). 2) Creating a new channel create transaction from scratch (U6).",
            "most_likely_effort": 3
        },
        {
            "activity_id": "A9",
            "activity_name": "Comprehensive Unit Testing",
            "activity_description": "Write unit tests for all public functions (U1-U4, U7, U8). Use mock/test protobuf config data. Cover happy paths, error conditions (e.g., org not found, invalid cert), and edge cases.",
            "most_likely_effort": 4
        },
        {
            "activity_id": "A10",
            "activity_name": "Integration Test & Example Application",
            "activity_description": "Create a complete, runnable example application or a integration test that sequences several operations (e.g., add anchor, then retrieve it) to verify end-to-end library functionality as described in the user stories.",
            "most_likely_effort": 2
        },
        {
            "activity_id": "A11",
            "activity_name": "Final Review & Polish",
            "activity_description": "Conduct a final code review, ensure all tests pass, refine documentation comments, and package the library for release (e.g., update go.mod, add a README if necessary).",
            "most_likely_effort": 1
        }
    ],
    "reported_total": {
        "most_likely_effort": 23
    }
}
```

